==== Hardware Serial Interface ====

| PIN   | NO PIN   | PIN   | PIN   | PIN   |
| *     | -        | *     | *     | *     |
| GND   | N/A      | RX    | TX    | VCC   |

:!: NEVER CONNECT THE VCC PIN. ONLY connect GND, RX and TX.

^ Serial connection parameters | 3.3V, 115200 Baud |

===== Preparation =====
==== Hardware ====
  * 3.3V USB to serial adapter 
  * USB stick (FAT16 formatted, single partition)
:!: There seem to be different root causes in case your USB stick is not detected correctly
  * Up to date USB sticks were not detected correctly by the stock U-Boot. I had to use the "oldest" USB Stick I found, which supports USB 1.1 only! [[https://forum.openwrt.org/t/serial-install-problems-on-nsa310/37306/11|OpenWrt Forum serial-install-problems-on-nsa310]]
  * A active USB Hub (with external power supply) might be necessary [[https://forum.doozan.com/read.php?3,119919,119964|doozan.com]]
  * Two USB sticks might be needed. One to flash the U-Boot. The second one to flash the OpenWrt image. [[https://forum.doozan.com/read.php?3,119919,119964|doozan.com]]

Alternative: Use [[docs:guide-user:troubleshooting:tftpserver|Setting up a TFTP server for TFTP Recovery/Install]] plus the description [[https://forum.openwrt.org/t/serial-install-problems-on-nsa310/37306/11|OpenWrt Forum - TFTP settings]] (no successful report found) or the flashing through IDE interface ([[https://forum.openwrt.org/t/serial-install-problems-on-nsa310/37306/44|tested successfully]]).

